 performs reads and writes asynchronously, and allows you to send and receive messages that contain both binary frames and UTF-8 encoded text frames. The task enqueues any reads or writes you perform prior to the handshake’s completion, and executes them after the handshake completes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentation\/Foundation\/URLSessionWebSocketTask","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" supports redirection and authentication like other types of tasks do, using the methods in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentation\/Foundation\/URLSessionTaskDelegate","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". The WebSocket task calls the redirection and authentication delegate methods prior to completing the handshake. The WebSocket task also supports cookies, by storing cookies to the session configuration’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentation\/Foundation\/URLSessionConfiguration\/httpCookieStorage","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and attaches cookies to outgoing HTTP handshake requests.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"watchOS supports ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentation\/Foundation\/URLSessionWebSocketTask","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for specific use cases. For more details, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Technotes\/tn3135-low-level-networking-on-watchOS","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentation\/Foundation\/URLSessionTask"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom"},{"id